[FINAL-TEXT] The evidence is conclusive. I have everything needed for the final diagnosis.

- `show interface eth0` on router1: **"Interface eth0 is down", Link ups: 0, last: (never)** — the interface has *never* come up since the lab started; `protodown: off` confirms FRR itself did not administratively shut it.
- BGP neighbor detail: `BGP state = Active`, `Last reset … No path to specified Neighbor`, `Connections established 1; dropped 1` — one brief flap then permanent failure because the link never recovered.
- Router1's routing table has no `193.10.11.0/24` connected route; router2 has it and has received one BGP prefix from router1 (from the brief window the session was up), but router1 received zero prefixes → no route to 200.1.1.0/24 → pc1 gets *Destination Net Unreachable*.

